{
  "bridge_text": "With the mossy floor cradling the little light, the robin-sized firefly flickered weakly as Mosk stood frozen by his old regret. The weight of those winters past hung heavy in the air, yet Lina sensed a change was finally at hand.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs, the humming settled into a quiet song. A firefly the size of a robin lay upon a bed of soft, velvet-green moss, her glow dimming like a dying ember. Mosk’s whiskers trembled as he looked down at her. He whispered that she had been his dearest friend once, but long ago, he had failed to bring her medicine in time. He had kept watch over this hollow tree ever since, too ashamed of his old mistake to ever truly face her again."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
