{
  "bridge_text": "The old fox Mosk watched Lina with eyes as sharp as needles, his green vest dusty from years of sitting in the dark. He waited to see what she would do next.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow tree, a staircase spiraled down into the shadows. Perched on the highest step sat an old grey fox wearing a vest of patched green cloth. This was Mosk. With a voice that sounded like dry leaves skittering on pavement, he told Lina that the tree was no place for a visitor. He insisted she go home and forget the strange humming she had heard. Lina looked at him steadily, replying that she could never forget a melody she had not yet truly heard."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
